Problem Statement

You are given two integers L and U representing a range [L, U] (inclusive).
Your task is to count how many numbers in this range consist of all unique digits, i.e., no digit is repeated within the number.

Input Format

Two integers L and U

Output Format

Print a single integer representing the count of numbers with all unique digits in the given range.

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

def count_unique_digits(lower, upper):
    count = 0

    for num in range(lower, upper + 1):
        s = str(num)
        if len(s) == len(set(s)):
            count += 1

    return count

